{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve for \\(a + b\\) given the equations \\(a^2b^3 = \\frac{32}{27}\\) and \\(\\frac{a}{b^3} = \\frac{27}{4}\\), we will proceed step by step.\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the second equation in a more convenient form:\n\\[\n\\frac{a}{b^3} = \\frac{27}{4} \\implies a = \\frac{27}{4} b^3\n\\]\n\nNext, substitute \\(a = \\frac{27}{4} b^3\\) into the first equation \\(a^2 b^3 = \\frac{32}{27}\\):\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{27}{4} b^3 \\right)^2 b^3 = \\frac{32}{27}\n\\]\n\nSimplify the left-hand side:\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{27}{4} \\right)^2 (b^3)^2 b^3 = \\frac{32}{27}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{729}{16} \\right) b^6 = \\frac{32}{27}\n\\]\n\nTo isolate \\(b^6\\), multiply both sides by \\(\\frac{16}{729}\\):\n\\[\nb^6 = \\frac{32}{27} \\cdot \\frac{16}{729}\n\\]\n\\[\nb^6 = \\frac{32 \\cdot 16}{27 \\cdot 729}\n\\]\n\\[\nb^6 = \\frac{512}{19683}\n\\]\n\nSimplify the fraction:\n\\[\nb^6 = \\left( \\frac{8}{27} \\right)^2\n\\]\n\nTaking the sixth root of both sides, we get:\n\\[\nb = \\pm \\frac{8}{27}\n\\]\n\n","prefix_end":904,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,369,17767,64,488,293,57758,2661,279,37906,17767,64,61,17,65,61,18,284,1124,37018,90,18,17,15170,17,22,11035,8,323,1124,11520,37018,90,64,15170,65,61,18,92,284,1124,37018,90,17,22,15170,19,11035,701,582,686,10354,3019,553,3019,382,5338,11,1077,594,18130,279,2086,23606,304,264,803,16710,1352,510,59,9640,59,37018,90,64,15170,65,61,18,92,284,1124,37018,90,17,22,15170,19,92,1124,6383,550,264,284,1124,37018,90,17,22,15170,19,92,293,61,18,198,59,2533,5847,11,27679,17767,64,284,1124,37018,90,17,22,15170,19,92,293,61,18,57758,1119,279,1156,23606,17767,64,61,17,293,61,18,284,1124,37018,90,18,17,15170,17,22,11035,982,59,9640,59,2359,7,1124,37018,90,17,22,15170,19,92,293,61,18,1124,1291,29776,17,293,61,18,284,1124,37018,90,18,17,15170,17,22,532,59,2533,50,70206,279,2115